2026-10-04|Total Perimeter of Figures Formed by 1s

Humanized Description of the Problem
We are given a binary matrix where `1` represents a filled cell and `0` represents an empty cell.
Every `1` cell initially contributes 4 sides to the perimeter. However, if two `1` cells share a side, that shared side is inside the figure and should not be counted as perimeter.
So, we can calculate the perimeter by checking each `1` cell and counting how many of its four sides touch either the boundary of the matrix or a `0`.

Question
Given a binary matrix `mat[][]` of size `n × m`, find the total perimeter of all figures formed by cells containing `1s`.
A single `1` cell has perimeter 4. Two horizontally or vertically adjacent `1` cells together have perimeter 6.

Approach
1. Traverse every cell of the matrix.
2. Whenever `mat[i][j] == 1`, initially add 4 to the answer.
3. Check its four neighboring cells:
   - Up: `(i - 1, j)`
   - Down: `(i + 1, j)`
   - Left: `(i, j - 1)`
   - Right: `(i, j + 1)`

4. If a neighboring cell also contains `1`, the two cells share one side. That side should not contribute to the perimeter, so subtract 1.
5. We can also avoid checking all four directions by only checking the top and left neighbors. Every shared edge will then be counted exactly once.
6. For each `1` cell:
   - Add 4.
   - If the cell above is `1`, subtract 1.
   - If the cell to the left is `1`, subtract 1.
7. Time complexity is O(n × m), since every matrix cell is visited once.
8. Space complexity is O(1), excluding the input matrix.

Solution
#include <bits/stdc++.h>
using namespace std;

int totalPerimeter(vector<vector<int>>& mat) {
    int n = mat.size();
    int m = mat[0].size();

    int perimeter = 0;

    for (int i = 0; i < n; i++) {
        for (int j = 0; j < m; j++) {
            if (mat[i][j] == 1) {
                perimeter += 4;

                // Shared side with the cell above
                if (i > 0 && mat[i - 1][j] == 1) {
                    perimeter--;
                }

                // Shared side with the cell on the left
                if (j > 0 && mat[i][j - 1] == 1) {
                    perimeter--;
                }
            }
        }
    }

    return perimeter;
}
